{"kind":"project","sections":[{"estimatedTimeInMinutes":20,"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Deliver Reminders to the user by formatting them and printing them to the terminal."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"title":"Delivering Reminders","backgroundImage":"1-0-0.png","kind":"hero","image":"1-0-0.png","chapter":"What's in a Reminder?"},{"tasks":[{"stepsSection":[{"caption":[],"type":"step","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Create a new ReminderManager.swift file."}]}],"code":"2-1-1.swift","media":null,"runtimePreview":null},{"caption":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"By setting this property to private, you can prevent other developers from making "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ReminderManager"},{"text":" remove a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Reminder","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" when they shouldn’t."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"step","code":"2-1-2.swift","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add a variable stored property, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reminders"},{"text":" to the ","type":"text"},{"code":"ReminderManager","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so it can track the Reminders."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"media":null,"runtimePreview":null},{"runtimePreview":null,"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Create a function to add Reminders to your ","type":"text"},{"code":"reminders","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" collection."}]}],"caption":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because we don’t want others modifying our "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reminders"},{"type":"text","text":" externally in whatever way they want, we’ll need to “wrap” one of the functions of that property with one of our own. This is a fairly common pattern when building containers on top of other containers, and is similar to (but not quite) the Decorator pattern."}]}],"type":"step","media":null,"code":"2-1-3.swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"